    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353-a2">

                <pb facs="0651" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg581"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 543.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Langston to Mr. Damier.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-04-04"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 4,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: While reserving all rights which may
                    pertain, under the circumstances, to any citizen of the United States being or
                    residing in Miragoâne, I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt, at 12
                    o’clock last night, of your dispatch dated the 3d instant, in which you announce
                    the purpose of your Government to bombard the city of Miragoâne after a notice
                    of twenty-four hours to the insurgents there assembled.</p>
                <p>As at present advised, Mr. Minister, I am of the opinion that no shooting as
                    indicated by you has taken place against the troops of the Government of Hayti
                    from any American vessels lying in the harbor of Miragoâne.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN MERCER LANGSTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
